        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "203539a6-b07b-5ca7-aede-7b2e98683f6a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Danie Visser, Oliver Marach, Rick Leach, Jim Pugh, Grant Connell, Glenn Michibata, Pieter Aldrich\n- Events: 1990 Australian Open – Men's Doubles\n- Topics: men's doubles rankings, Grand Slam men's doubles titles\n\nFacts:\n- On October 18, 2010, Oliver Marach reached his career-high doubles ranking of world No. 8.\n- In the 1990 Australian Open – Men's Doubles, defending champions Rick Leach and Jim Pugh lost in the semifinals to Grant Connell and Glenn Michibata.\n- In the 1990 Australian Open – Men's Doubles final, Pieter Aldrich and Danie Visser defeated Grant Connell and Glenn Michibata 6–4, 4–6, 6–1, 6–4 to win the title.\n- Danie Visser was a doubles specialist who won three Grand Slam men's doubles titles, including two Australian Open titles and one US Open title.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d3150ba4-cea8-5dfc-ac20-a51673548d55",
        "text": "Page: Danie Visser. Sentence: A doubles specialist, he won 3 Grand Slam men's doubles titles (2 Australian Open and 1 US Open).\nPage: Oliver Marach. Sentence: His career high in doubles is world No. 8, set on October 18, 2010.\nPage: 1990 Australian Open – Men's Doubles. Sentence: Rick Leach and Jim Pugh were the defending champions, but lost in the semifinals to Grant Connell and Glenn Michibata.\nPage: 1990 Australian Open – Men's Doubles. Sentence: Pieter Aldrich and Danie Visser won the title, defeating Connell and Michibata 6–4, 4–6, 6–1, 6–4, in the final.",
